  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">COMMUNITY-BASED SEA TURTLE CONSERVATION ON MAIO ISLAND, CAPE VERDE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO IMPLEMENT NESTING BEACH CONSERVATION PROGRAMS FOR THE LOGGERHEAD ON THE ISLAND OF MAIO. MAIO HAS THE SECOND-LARGEST LOGGERHEAD NESTING POPULATION IN CAPE VERDE AND IS ONE OF THE LEAST DEVELOPED ISLANDS. ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: 1. COMMUNITY-BASED NIGHTTIME SURVEYS THROUGHOUT THE NESTING SEASON ON THE SIX MOST IMPORTANT NESTING BEACHES 2. AN OUTREACH PROGRAM FOCUSED ON ASSISTING LOCAL FISHERMEN WITH DEVELOPING ALTERNATIVE LIVELIHOODS AND INTEGRATING THEM INTO THE CONSERVATION PROGRAM INCLUDING A GUARDIANS OF THE SEA PROGRAM AND (3) AN EXTENSIVE COMMUNITY EDUCATION OUTREACH PROGRAM TO ENGAGE THE 12 MAIN LOCAL COMMUNITIES IN SEA TURTLE CONSERVATION ISSUES AND SOLUTIONS.</narrative>
  </description>
